WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.730
What Hachijou-senpai does every day?

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.150
You wanted to talk to me?

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:14.940
That's right.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:15.990
What is it?

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.770
I wanted to ask you something 
about Hachijou-senpai!

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:19.620
You're too close.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.450
Well? What is it?

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:28.200
Do you think Hachijou-senpai would 
take my questions seriously?

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.140
You mean Bird?

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.090
Then it doesn't matter whether 
you're the one asking.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.040
What matters is whether it entertains him.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.850
So I just need to be sure 
it entertains him, right?

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.640
Please make me your partner!

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.560
Huh?

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.890
It's okay, right?

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.160
I'll get permission from Public Safety.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.320
B-But the boss will...

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.500
My sister has nothing to do with this.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.470
It's my decision.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.430
All right.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:55.490
Hey, Jirou!

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.780
First, I want you to do something for me.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.740
Give me a list of Bird's actions, 
his statements, his decisions...

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.410
Everything you know about him.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.920
I have no idea what his daily life is like.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.970
Sis!

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.600
I'm going to get dinner started.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.970
Okay!

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.100
So this is where it was...

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.760
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.340
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.470
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.820
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.110
<b>File 10: A Farewell Banquet</b>

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.050
Jirou says that when he worked as part of Logos,

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:02.570
several things were done 
that he didn't know about.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.300
But then the ass said that if Bird 
were working with Inagi-san,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.580
it'd make sense...

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.330
That's absurd!

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.500
Inagi-san would never do that.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.890
How are things proceeding with the summit?

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:16.710
Right...

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:22.680
<b>Anyone Can Go to Space 
Everyone Will Go to Space 
Space Elevator: From Tokyo to Space</b>

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:22.680
<b>The First Step Toward a New Era 
Let's Make the Tokyo City 
Summit a Success!</b>

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.850
Governor, it appears that, due to 
your overwhelming approval rating,

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:22.680
no one could easily intervene.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.030
What about the space elevator?

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.620
No issues there.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.630
If this test works,

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:31.410
the project will de facto belong to us.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.240
I see.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:33.730
Proceed, then.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:34.450
Yes, sir.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.710
At this rate, I may be able to increase the 
speed of the city development plan.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.790
You?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.550
Hey there, Governor.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:44.450
How are you?

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:48.540
I asked you not to contact me here.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.410
And that icon is far too dangerous!

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.340
Don't worry. I've taken precautions.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.580
More importantly, things seem to be going well.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.460
So you're watching me?

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.790
Don't worry.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:02.800
It's just an insurance policy.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.970
You're concerned that being attached to 
the Carupanuba Embassy won't suffice?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.020
Insurance is important, isn't it?

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.390
Did you call to talk about nothing?

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.500
Sorry, sorry. I'll get to the point.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.070
Your city development plan is beautiful, 
but it's not very entertaining.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.510
I'm not interested in your opinion.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.530
So I came up with this one instead!

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.710
What do you think?

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.200
This is madness... Are you serious?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.690
Entertaining, right?

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:33.910
It's insane!

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.720
You're a mad devil!

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.170
And you sold that devil your soul, 
so you don't get to complain.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:44.810
I know. Come up with something more 
entertaining, and maybe I'll stop!

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:49.640
Chinju!

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.140
Are you here, Chinju?

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:52.990
Excuse me.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.650
Get approval for Item B.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.140
Understood.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.570
If you'd like...

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.280
Here you go.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:06.740
What did you learn?

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.760
I've already told you many times.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.200
Bird is working with the governor.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.590
What's your proof?

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:15.160
And is there a reason that 
they'd work together?

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.370
I've known him forever, you know.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:19.540
Sorry, but I don't find your theory—

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.340
Because you believe in him blindly.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.510
What did you say?!

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.930
More importantly, Bird is incredibly smart.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.310
He pretended to be my right arm

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.700
while he found another left arm for himself.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.350
And that's Inagi-san?

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.870
That's impossible!

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:33.810
But...

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:37.080
Knowing Senpai's personality, it's very possible

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.270
that he'd prepare a second 
person as insurance.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.820
I'm not quite done,

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.940
but here's the information you requested.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.790
I have movie data, as well.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:47.650
Thanks.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.830
I knew it.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:57.610
Look through the documents again 
to see if there's anything in it for him.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.170
No matter how many times 
I do, it'll be the same.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:03.110
Given the chance, a talented person 
can get good results in any situation.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:07.700
But he's been given far too many 
chances in a very short time.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.570
Don't tell me you never found that strange.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.220
I'm sure Public Safety is also suspicious.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.560
Otherwise they'd never let me look into this.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.060
So he knows, huh?

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:22.620
I should have never told you about 
Inagi-san in the first place!

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.050
You're going to pretend ignorance?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.980
The governor deliberately allowed 
crimes to be committed

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.120
in order to achieve his ideals.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.040
Is my sister going to be okay?

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:38.170
If what Shimajirou-san says is true...

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.960
It's still only a hypothesis. Don't worry about it.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.980
Actually, on her last day off...

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.060
Sis, dinner's gonna get col—

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.800
Whoa, what the heck happened?!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.100
Why is your room so messy?

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.640
I-It's fine, I'm not making 
a mess. I'm cleaning up.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:56.960
You're lying.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.510
You'd definitely ask me for 
help if you were cleaning!

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.350
No, not today.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.790
What's this box?

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:03.790
Oh, that's...

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.350
A wedding dress?

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.390
Why? Why?

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:08.740
Oh, well...

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:12.200
Um... I was a silly young girl once.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.890
Wait, you were a cosplayer?

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.020
No!

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.790
Then why?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.510
You were little, so you probably don't know this,

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.950
but I almost married Inagi-kun.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:25.750
Seriously?!

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:26.550
Yes.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.970
I mean, I tried to get the truth 
out of her a few times...

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.300
But I didn't imagine they were that close.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:34.640
So...

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.550
All right!

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.420
Sorry for coming unannounced.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.360
Jirou was being stupid.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.670
Not really.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:43.840
I thought it was possible, as well.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:44.750
You, too?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.300
I got a message from PS a while ago.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.450
From Public Safety?

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.610
About Inagi-san, not Jirou?

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.490
Yeah.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:56.830
<b>Extra Spicy Chinese Restaurant 
Nyan Ma La</b>

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.780
Welcome!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.830
I'm Yamabuki. I have a reservation 
for the "liver and onion feast."

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.580
We've been waiting!

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.000
This way.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.270
Hey, Madoka-chan!

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:12.010
Yo.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.840
So, about the job...

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.840
How about that job?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:15.650
Sorry.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:19.140
I wanted to be sure it wasn't true, 
so I asked Madoka-chan a while ago.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.630
Seriously?

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:22.140
I'll tell you up-front

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:27.400
that I couldn't find any evidence linking 
Governor Inagi to the crimes.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.370
I see.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:32.240
Instead, I was astonished by 
his leadership qualities.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.470
I can see

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.570
why you almost married him, boss.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.850
You figured that out, too?

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.660
It's not too late.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.770
No way! Too much time has passed.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:46.360
By the way, Madoka, did you investigate 
Fuang Chuan and Neohei?

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.190
The new Chinese mafia groups?

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.500
Jirou keeps telling me to look into them.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.210
I hadn't thought of that.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.690
Sorry. Just when you were finally sure...

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.200
No, at this point, I want to be certain.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.070
Yeah.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.630
What is it, Inagi-kun?

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.600
I wanted to see your face.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:12.130
Huh?

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.690
Well, I'll be on my way.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.570
Ten days until the Tokyo City Summit...

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:21.190
My great dream is finally about 
to reach the starting line.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:24.910
From now on, the world should 
be organized around cities.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.600
That's what you said in your book, right?

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.500
I think that would be amazing.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:30.410
Yeah.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.510
I'll make it a reality.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.420
And for that to happen...

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.970
Rin, I want you to be my wife.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:38.970
Huh?

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:44.630
I realized how much I need you.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.290
Where did this come from?

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.380
I know it's selfish.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.540
But it's still my unwavering ideal.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:54.070
Come in.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:57.350
A political upheaval has occurred at home.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:59.250
The Politburo head has been 
driven from power.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.780
Okay, then...

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.700
I see... So you heard him?

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:07.010
I'm sorry.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:11.380
If Inagi-san was involved in 
some huge conspiracy,

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.370
I wanted to help him.

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.920
I'm a terrible woman, aren't I?

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:21.390
I'm suspicious of someone who's 
proposed to me twice.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.100
Inagi-kun hasn't changed.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.680
Yeah, that's true.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.000
Yeah.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.230
He was just as honest last time, too...

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.640
What? Come with you to America?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:36.310
Yeah. Naganuma-sensei did a lot of work,

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.760
and I'll be able to take part in 
a political exchange program.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.480
I'll never have a chance like this again, so...

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:45.400
I want you to accompany me as my wife.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:50.240
But I'm supposed to go to the 
National Police Agency...

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.770
I know it's selfish.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:54.680
But going with you is my ideal.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.760
I thought about it for a long time,

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.690
but we both ended up deciding 
to follow our own dreams,

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:03.780
and in the end...

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.560
So that's what happened.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:09.050
It may be he's being forced 
to make a big decision.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.780
I don't know whether it's good or bad.

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:14.070
But he's always come to me

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:17.650
whenever he wasn't entirely sure what to do.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.180
So maybe this is also...

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.280
It has to be a good thing!

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:25.700
He's the person who gave me 
a path to follow in life.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.860
He hasn't changed.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.620
This time, he'll give everyone a path to follow.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.330
A path to follow, huh?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.030
Yes!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.270
"Miho, I've thought about this many times,

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.400
but I could only come to one conclusion.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.040
I'm happy you like me,

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.710
but I just can't imagine us 
sharing a future together.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:57.480
<b>Subject: For Our Future</b>

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.480
So I'm very sorry, but I don't think

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.700
we should see each other anymore."

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.700
I see...

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.120
An interesting point.

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:04.770
Yes, it's a critical turning point for the governor.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:02.910
<b>Send</b>

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.200
It's the City Summit, after all.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.760
That's the starting point.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.820
In fact, the turning point is before that...

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.330
How does he deal with things 
that could prevent its start?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.530
In simpler terms, how does he silence Bird?

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:18.290
Hey!

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:22.260
I thought that Inagi-san working 
with Hachijou was only a hypothesis!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.730
Would you please be quiet?!

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:27.010
I'm about to decide to hit the go-ahead button

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.350
on an extremely important matter!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.060
What's up?

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.310
I was looking into the Chinese mafia,

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:38.340
and I got a message from a mysterious woman.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:38.860
A woman?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.640
I don't know who she is, but she 
claimed she has interesting data.

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:44.630
Be careful.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.360
All right.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.080
Someone was watching.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:50.460
They were told to give the documents 
to whoever came looking for them.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.280
Yeah.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:54.470
Is it you?

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:55.030
Yeah.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:58.790
I was told to give this to you.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.260
Where did you get this?

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.460
A designated coin locker.

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:05.130
From whom?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.140
No idea.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.940
They instructed me over the Internet.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:08.620
Bye.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.280
A snake?

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.730
What is this?

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:15.190
It seems like an icon...

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:18.590
I'll open the video file that's in here with it.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:21.110
Kobari-san?!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.650
What's this doing here?

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:26.280
Wasn't he the one who tried 
to attack the last governor?

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:26.820
Yeah.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:28.660
He's dead now, though.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:31.550
I'll play the video.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.470
<i>Wh-Who are you?</i>

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:36.970
<i>All I'll say is that I'm someone who 
knows Governor Terao well.</i>

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.490
<i>I'll be giving you instructions now.</i>

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:40.290
<i>The representative?</i>

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.350
<i>You found the Willwear?</i>

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:44.750
This is a conversation between 
the client and the criminal?

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:43.650
<i>Y-Yes...</i>

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:47.090
<i>All right. I've already told you 
the governor's demands.</i>

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:45.640
Probably.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.510
The client's voice is heavily filtered.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.510
<i>And my daughter?</i>

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.790
I'll see if I can clean it up.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.330
<i>I'll give you my full support.</i>

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:55.660
<i>But you are not to speak a word, other than 
about your relationship with Naganuma.</i>

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.200
<i>That is my condition.</i>

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.710
<i>You'll really keep your promise?</i>

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:01.040
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.940
<i>No matter what, take this and head 
for the Tokyo government office.</i>

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.220
Inagi-san...

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:10.120
But this isn't enough to...

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.330
No, I haven't tested it for alterations,

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.950
so it can't be submitted as evidence yet.

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:18.120
Kuroki-kun...

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.540
Whose shot was that?

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.000
It wasn't us.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:26.880
Hey, is that...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.260
<b>Conference Room</b>

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.260
The bill has passed

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:34.220
by a majority vote!

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.690
Hachijou committed suicide?!

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.150
That's impossible!

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:45.060
But the body's DNA matches 
Hachijou's from the store.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:48.250
He appears to have had Carupanuba citizenship,

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:52.660
but his sponsor lost power during 
a recent political upheaval.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:57.950
He'd been ordered to return home, 
and it was clear he'd be executed if he did.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.770
I understand.

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:01.520
Chief...

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.080
The data analysis you requested.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.070
Thank you.

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:05.790
Data?

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:06.460
Yes.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:10.260
It was data copied from Governor 
Inagi's secretary's computer.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.010
Is that legal?

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.710
I had the managing director 
restore the deleted data,

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:18.230
and it contained this.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:20.800
Impossible!

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.060
It must be some mistake!

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.730
I'll talk to Inagi-san and find out for myself!

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.190
Wait, Kuroki-kun.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.350
Calm down.

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:33.070
If that incident connected Inagi-kun to Logos,

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.830
then Hachijou's suicide may have 
been as Shimajirou-kun said.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.950
Now you're saying that, boss?!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.040
Right now, I'm speaking

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.850
not as his friend, but as a police officer.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:47.880
But...

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:52.090
There's no way to verify the 
truth of Hachijou's suicide.

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:53.850
Carupanuba is currently

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:57.470
the country the Japanese government 
has the most concerns about.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:00.520
Did you find anything, Hayashida-san?

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.640
Any evidence?

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:02.700
Of course not.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.200
If we had, we would've already...

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.160
"When in doubt, find for the accused."

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.490
Boss, I'm going to follow police principles.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.250
Yes.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.410
Everyone, help me.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.010
I have an idea.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:22.670
I'm sorry to call you here this late, Inagi-kun.

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:26.040
I'd never refuse anything you wanted.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.140
Thank you.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:31.760
But next time, I'd like to know 
what we're doing in advance.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:34.740
I'm still wearing my usual clothes.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.820
I'm sorry.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.830
You're very pretty, Rin.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.830
The boss looks beautiful.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.020
Yes.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:51.040
But was this really the only way?

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.610
There must be no lies in love.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:17:00.230
Inagi Koutaro-san, you are about 
to marry Yamabuki Rin-san.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:05.440
Do you promise to answer your wife's 
questions truthfully, without lies?

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:06.880
I do.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:09.920
Let us hear the bride's words to the groom.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.720
I never thought I would stand 
next to you, wearing this.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.880
Neither did I.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.680
Thank you, Rin.

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:22.770
Inagi-kun, answer what I'm about 
to ask you without lying.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:29.210
You've heard about the death of Logos's 
Bird, AKA Hachijou Tomoki, right?

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:29.840
Yes.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:31.690
I'm told it was suicide.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:35.450
But the first message the Carupanuba 
Embassy sent to Azabu Station

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.950
was that someone was trying to break in.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.830
But before the police could head 
out, they received a retraction.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:44.570
Then they were told one of the 
staff had committed suicide.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.250
What do you suspect?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:51.300
Did you hire the Chinese mafia 
to attack the embassy?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.510
Wait... Where is this coming from?

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.580
You needed the power of Hachijou,

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.190
the man behind the Logos Incident.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:03.220
Even after becoming governor, 
you offered him a Willwear,

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:07.350
allowing him to commit crimes 
to further your ideals.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:12.080
But I didn't need him anymore, 
so I got rid of him, is that it?

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.370
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:16.730
<i>No matter what, take this and head 
for the Tokyo government office.</i>

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:18.660
This is your voice, isn't it?

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:20.620
It does sound like me.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.770
This is the image file given to 
us with the voice data.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:28.330
It's probably the icon of the 
one giving Kobari-san orders.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:33.800
The exact same icon was recovered 
from your secretary's PC.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.950
Even if that's me talking to Kobari-san, I'm only

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:39.280
telling him to go to the Tokyo City office.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:43.300
I'm only an intermediary who doesn't 
know the details of the contract,

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:46.020
reminding him that he needs 
to keep his end of the deal.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:47.730
Then what about this?

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.480
During the incident at Atami,

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:54.440
you happened to be in some 
of the peeping tom's photos.

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:59.320
Evidently, you're talking to the criminal 
underworld's third most important man.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:02.530
We used lip-reading to make 
out the conversation.

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:04.400
This is what you said.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.490
"The stealth type is ready, yes?

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.700
Perhaps the Yamanote Immigrant District..."

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.540
You used that to tempt the 
former Carupanuba official

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.210
into attacking civilians, didn't you?

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.550
When you're governor, you meet many people.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:23.860
I can't investigate all of their personal histories, 
but I'll be careful from now on.

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:26.860
And I seem to remember that lip-reading

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:29.900
has an accuracy rating around thirty percent.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:33.020
That's how you set everything up, right?

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.500
But now, at the worst possible time,

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:38.770
Hachijou Tomoki said something 
far beyond your expectations.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.580
You couldn't go along, of course.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:47.070
So you fretted a while, before setting in 
motion the backup plan you'd prepared.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:48.330
That was...

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.500
The assassination of Hachijou Tomoki.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.220
Yes.

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:54.930
Depending on its success, your fate 
would change dramatically.

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:58.910
That was why you came to me.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:00.840
Do you have proof?

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.240
My intuition.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:04.550
So feel free to deny it.

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:08.020
But please don't lie to me here.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.230
Just as I'd expect from you, Rin.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:12.350
You're correct.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:17.570
But legally, how much can be done to me?

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.650
Including all of the later Willwear incidents?

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:24.410
I simply told him my plan as governor.

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:27.580
Hachijou-kun arranged everything 
without a word from me.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:30.190
He was quite considerate.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.040
So you maintain your actions were legal?

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.150
What evidence do you have?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.980
In a country of laws,

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:39.050
if a thing can't be prosecuted, it may 
as well have never happened.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:43.350
You were the top graduate of the legal 
department, so you know that well.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.760
Please! Turn yourself in, Inagi-kun!

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:48.430
There's no need, and it's impossible.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:52.980
I'm a talented and incredibly popular governor.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.270
And for all those people to be happy,

00:20:56.270 --> 00:21:00.030
you have no choice but to give me both 
your public and private selves.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.660
It's almost time for the City Summit, 
my moment to shine.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.080
Inagi, you bastard!

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:06.570
Oh?

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:08.750
Not "Inagi-san" this time, Kuroki?

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.410
You must be an important man now.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.620
Shut up!

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:14.250
In my mind, I've always supported you!

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.460
But you...

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:16.830
Don't worry.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.720
I'm willing to call this a training exercise.

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:21.710
I'll expose what you did!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.090
You're the same as Rin.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:27.430
You've inherited a set of laws, 
and all you do is uphold them.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.530
For the betterment of Japan... no,

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:33.440
for the whole world, I will change society.

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:35.830
My role as a human being is different.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.140
To hell with that!

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:39.920
No matter what your ideals, 
what's wrong is wrong!

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:42.110
I'll never forgive you for this!

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:44.580
You never grow up.

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:47.990
No one is left to stand in my way.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:48.910
Kuroki-kun!

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:49.510
Farewell.

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:50.030
Kuroki-kun!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:50.840
Kuroki-san!

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:52.610
This was quite an entertaining diversion.

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:57.900
He's awake!

00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:01.950
Kuroki-san, do you know where you are?

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:05.440
What's Jirou doing here?

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:08.010
Hayashida-san, huh?

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:09.940
Tricky old bastard...

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:12.270
What do you want to do to the governor?

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:15.080
Jeez.

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:17.950
You should never worship idols.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:22.310
I was an idol once, so I know 
what I'm talking about.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:56.120
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:56.360
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:23:56.120 --> 00:24:09.040
File 11: Dream of an Idol

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.430
No, this isn't the time for cheerful greetings!

00:23:58.430 --> 00:23:59.720
Then I'll do it.

00:23:59.720 --> 00:24:00.950
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:24:00.950 --> 00:24:02.220
Hayashida-san from Public Safety?!

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:03.320
That was unexpected!

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:04.840
Next time, more unexpected events await.

00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:07.280
W-Wait, are you the final boss?!
